WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:05.589
San Diego Comic-Con has revealed some super-special
news for the CW's Arrowverse - and it's a

00:00:05.589 --> 00:00:07.910
development we never thought we'd ever see.

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:11.900
A familiar face is donning Superman's cape
once again, and he has some feelings about

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:13.260
the impending comeback.

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:18.140
As part of the festivities of Comic-Con 2019,
it was announced that the CW is cooking up

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:23.390
a crossover of epic proportions: former Superman
actor Brandon Routh, who played Clark Kent

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:28.630
in the 2006 film Superman Returns, and current
Man of Steel Tyler Hoechlin, who portrays

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:32.850
Supes in a recurring capacity on Supergirl,
will both be suiting up as Superman as a part

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:36.420
of the Arrowverse's upcoming "Crisis on Infinite
Earths" event.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:41.329
It's a role Routh hasn't played since 2006's
Superman Returns, and at this point, almost

00:00:41.329 --> 00:00:43.879
certainly never expected to play again.

00:00:43.879 --> 00:00:45.800
"He was Superman.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:48.800
Everyone was in love with him."

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:54.100
The announcement, first reported by Deadline
on July 19, got fans in the best kind of huff:

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:59.280
a fast-talking frenzy that left some commenters
already declaring "Crisis on Infinite Earths"

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:01.649
as the greatest crossover event ever.

00:01:01.649 --> 00:01:05.800
Not long after the news hit the 'net, Routh
took to social media just like the fans did

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:07.800
to react to his return as Superman.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:10.470
"I think it's only fair that I answer."

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:14.640
Routh tweeted in response to Deadline's post
confirming the news, saying that he was

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:17.590
"Honored, humbled, grateful, and still pinching
myself."

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:22.530
Hoechlin, who first slipped into the Superman
suit in 2016 for Supergirl, expressed his

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:26.420
own anticipation for the forthcoming clash
of the Supermen by tweeting at Routh,

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:27.530
"Let's go brother!"

00:01:27.530 --> 00:01:31.420
Routh bantered back with a punch and a wink
emoji, as well as the comment,

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:34.390
"So excited to share the screen with you as
Supes @tylerhoechlin!

00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:35.390
So fun!

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:36.390
I'm so ready!"

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:39.960
Routh also joked that he was immediately heading
off to the gym to get into tip-top shape for

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:43.700
the crossover, though we doubt he actually
needs to, considering that he's been playing

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:45.730
superheroes for years.

00:01:45.730 --> 00:01:49.730
Arrowverse loyals will already recognize Routh
from his role as Ray Palmer, better known

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:54.670
as the Atom -- a role which he's taken to
Arrow, The Flash, and DC's Legends of Tomorrow,

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:56.490
on which he's currently a main player.

00:01:56.490 --> 00:02:00.170
The actor also opened up to Entertainment
Weekly about his return to the role that put

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:01.640
him on the map as a younger man.

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:05.560
He admitted that he initially experienced
mixed feelings about the news before letting

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:06.820
himself feel excited.

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:08.440
Asked about his outlook, Routh said,

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:12.101
"It's an opportunity for me to kind of say
hello and goodbye to the character in a way

00:02:12.101 --> 00:02:13.499
I didn't get to the first time."

00:02:13.499 --> 00:02:18.641
"Being a young individual of 24, 25, I thought,
'Oh, I'm going to do this for years and make

00:02:18.641 --> 00:02:19.641
multiple movies.'

00:02:19.641 --> 00:02:20.799
And that of course didn't happen.

00:02:20.799 --> 00:02:23.959
I'm just very honored to do this one last
time."

00:02:23.959 --> 00:02:27.920
Routh and Hoechlin's eagerness about playing
duelling Supermen is nothing compared to the

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:30.209
reactions of their fans, one of whom tweeted,

00:02:30.209 --> 00:02:34.099
"The fact that both of you will be sharing
the screen as Supes is blowing my mind!

00:02:34.099 --> 00:02:36.459
Can't wait to see you both back in the red
cape!"

00:02:36.459 --> 00:02:40.129
Another said that the news was the best thing
they had heard yet from this year's Comic-Con

00:02:40.129 --> 00:02:44.439
- even more incredible than the surprise Top
Gun: Maverick trailer Tom Cruise dropped on

00:02:44.439 --> 00:02:45.439
Thursday.

00:02:45.439 --> 00:02:46.439
According to that fan,

00:02:46.439 --> 00:02:50.480
"I was buzzing like a happy bee over the Top
Gun trailer… then this Brandon Routh news

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:54.150
drops into my hive like a dollop of sweet
unpasteurized honey.

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:55.150
Yes!

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:55.840
Yes!

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:56.320
Yes!

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:57.800
Best DC news in ever."

00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:01.840
What makes the news of Routh's return to the
Superman role so exciting is that many thought

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:03.209
it would never be possible.

00:03:03.209 --> 00:03:07.469
The idea of seeing Routh as Kal-El again was
pretty unthinkable after Superman Returns

00:03:07.469 --> 00:03:11.489
failed to generate the kind of box office
that studio Warner Brothers Pictures needed

00:03:11.489 --> 00:03:16.540
to greenlight a sequel, taking in just over
$391 million worldwide.

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:21.420
That's not much compared to other DC Comics-based
fare from WB, which has tended to scoop up

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:27.090
anywhere from around $750 million globally
on the lower end to over $1 billion at the

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:28.090
top.

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:32.139
While Routh did pick up praise for his performance,
Warner Bros. decided not to pursue more films

00:03:32.139 --> 00:03:33.150
with him in the role.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:37.980
The studio wound up rebooting the character
seven years later in 2013's Man of Steel,

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:41.260
the film that started the DC Extended Universe
as we know it.

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:45.900
It's unknown which installments of the five-episode
"Crisis on Infinite Earths" event Routh and

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:46.920
Hoechlin will appear on.

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:50.849
Much like previous crossover events in the
Arrowverse, the expansive story is set to

00:03:50.849 --> 00:03:55.859
once again bring together the casts of the
CW's superhero series, this time including

00:03:55.859 --> 00:03:59.739
Arrow, Batwoman, The Flash, Legends of Tomorrow,
and Supergirl.

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:03.200
Even without the Superman news, it's clear
that the event will be the biggest one in

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:08.090
the Arrowverse thus far, spanning two months
of real time, with three episodes of the crossover

00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:12.180
seeing release in December, and two more to
follow in January 2020.

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:16.979
The crossover's story is likely to follow,
or at least draw inspiration from, the DC

00:04:16.979 --> 00:04:21.400
Comics storyline of the same name, in which
the heroes fight against the nefarious Anti-Monitor

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:25.229
with the help of alternate versions of themselves
from different universes.

00:04:25.229 --> 00:04:29.340
With that story as a jumping off point, "Crisis
on Infinite Earths" was already shaping up

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:33.889
to be unlike anything Arrowverse fans had
seen prior to this announcement - but now,

00:04:33.889 --> 00:04:35.139
it's simply superb.

00:04:35.139 --> 00:04:39.190
Two Supermans at the same time is just the
icing on the cake, and we're glad that Routh

00:04:39.190 --> 00:04:41.880
thinks the news is as sweet as we do.

